"{\n  \"entry_block_ref\": \"check_npx\",\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Treat this skill as CLI-first automation.\",\n    \"Do not pivot to `@playwright/test` unless the user explicitly asks for test files.\",\n    \"Before proposing commands, check whether `npx` is available (the wrapper depends on it).\",\n    \"Once `npx` is present, proceed with the wrapper script. A global install of `playwright-cli` is optional.\",\n    \"Prefer the bundled wrapper script so the CLI works even when it is not globally installed.\",\n    \"Prefer the wrapper unless the repository already standardizes on a global install.\",\n    \"Use the wrapper script unless the CLI is already installed globally:\",\n    \"Default to CLI commands and workflows, not Playwright test specs.\",\n    \"Use the wrapper script and snapshot often.\",\n    \"In this repo, run commands from `output/playwright/<label>/` to keep artifacts contained.\",\n    \"If an element ref fails, run `pwcli snapshot` again and retry.\",\n    \"If the page looks wrong, re-open with `--headed` and resize the window.\",\n    \"By default, the CLI reads `playwright-cli.json` from the current directory. Use `--config` to point at a specific file.\"\n  ],\n  \"declared_context_keys\": [\n    \"PATH\",\n    \"CODEX_HOME\",\n    \"HOME\",\n    \"PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION\"\n  ],\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"check_npx\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Check whether npx is available\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"context\",\n      \"constraints\": [],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"check_npx_availability\",\n          \"opcode\": \"check_npx_availability\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"context_key\",\n              \"identifier\": \"PATH\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"npx_available\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"script_content\": \"command -v npx >/dev/null 2>&1\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_npx_check\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"npx_available\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"install_nodejs\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Ask the user to install Node.js/npm\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"ask_user_to_install_nodejs\",\n          \"opcode\": \"ask_user_to_install_nodejs\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"literal\",\n              \"literal_value\": \"# Verify Node/npm are installed\\nnode --version\\nnpm --version\\n\\n# If missing, install Node.js/npm, then:\\nnpm install -g @playwright/cli@latest\\nplaywright-cli --help\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [\n            \"Provide these steps verbatim.\"\n          ],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_install_request\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"setup_wrapper\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Set the bundled Playwright CLI wrapper path\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"context\",\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"User-scoped skills install under `$CODEX_HOME/skills` (default: `~/.codex/skills`).\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"resolve_pwcli_path\",\n          \"opcode\": \"set_playwright_cli_wrapper_path\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"context_key\",\n              \"identifier\": \"CODEX_HOME\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"context_key\",\n              \"identifier\": \"HOME\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"pwcli_path\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"script_content\": \"export CODEX_HOME=\\\"${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}\\\"\\nexport PWCLI=\\\"$CODEX_HOME/skills/playwright/scripts/playwright_cli.sh\\\"\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_setup\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"read_session_env\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Read the optional Playwright CLI session name\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"context\",\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"If a flow depends on prior state, use a named `--session`.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"read_playwright_cli_session\",\n          \"opcode\": \"read_playwright_cli_session\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"context_key\",\n              \"identifier\": \"PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"playwright_cli_session\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_session_read\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"choose_reference\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Choose reference guides to open as needed\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"Open only what you need: CLI command reference: `references/cli.md`; Practical workflows and troubleshooting: `references/workflows.md`.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"assess_reference_need\",\n          \"opcode\": \"assess_reference_need\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"needed_reference\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_reference_choice\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"needed_reference\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"read_cli_reference\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Read the CLI command reference\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"external\",\n      \"constraints\": [],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"read_cli_reference\",\n          \"opcode\": \"read_reference_guide\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"references/cli.md\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"cli_reference_content\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_cli_reference\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"read_workflows_reference\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Read the workflows and troubleshooting reference\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"external\",\n      \"constraints\": [],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"read_workflows_reference\",\n          \"opcode\": \"read_reference_guide\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"references/workflows.md\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"workflows_reference_content\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_workflows_reference\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"open_page\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Open the target browser page\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"Use `--headed` when a visual check will help.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"open_page\",\n          \"opcode\": \"execute_playwright_cli_wrapper\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"pwcli_path\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"literal\",\n              \"literal_value\": \"open\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"target_webpage\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"playwright_cli_session\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"script_content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nif ! command -v npx >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n  echo \\\"Error: npx is required but not found on PATH.\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nhas_session_flag=\\\"false\\\"\\nfor arg in \\\"$@\\\"; do\\n  case \\\"$arg\\\" in\\n    --session|--session=*)\\n      has_session_flag=\\\"true\\\"\\n      break\\n      ;;\\n  esac\\ndone\\n\\ncmd=(npx --yes --package @playwright/cli playwright-cli)\\nif [[ \\\"${has_session_flag}\\\" != \\\"true\\\" && -n \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION:-}\\\" ]]; then\\n  cmd+=(--session \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION}\\\")\\nfi\\ncmd+=(\\\"$@\\\")\\n\\nexec \\\"${cmd[@]}\\\"\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_open\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"snapshot_page\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Snapshot the page to obtain stable element refs\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"external\",\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"Always snapshot before referencing element ids like `e12`.\",\n        \"Re-snapshot when refs seem stale.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"take_browser_snapshot\",\n          \"opcode\": \"execute_playwright_cli_wrapper\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"pwcli_path\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"literal\",\n              \"literal_value\": \"snapshot\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"browser_session\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"playwright_cli_session\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"snapshot_refs\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"script_content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nif ! command -v npx >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n  echo \\\"Error: npx is required but not found on PATH.\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nhas_session_flag=\\\"false\\\"\\nfor arg in \\\"$@\\\"; do\\n  case \\\"$arg\\\" in\\n    --session|--session=*)\\n      has_session_flag=\\\"true\\\"\\n      break\\n      ;;\\n  esac\\ndone\\n\\ncmd=(npx --yes --package @playwright/cli playwright-cli)\\nif [[ \\\"${has_session_flag}\\\" != \\\"true\\\" && -n \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION:-}\\\" ]]; then\\n  cmd+=(--session \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION}\\\")\\nfi\\ncmd+=(\\\"$@\\\")\\n\\nexec \\\"${cmd[@]}\\\"\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_snapshot\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"interact_page\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Interact with the page using refs from the latest snapshot\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"Prefer explicit commands over `eval` and `run-code` unless needed.\",\n        \"When you do not have a fresh snapshot, use placeholder refs like `eX` and say why; do not bypass refs with `run-code`.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"interact_with_page\",\n          \"opcode\": \"execute_playwright_cli_wrapper\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"pwcli_path\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"literal\",\n              \"literal_value\": \"click/type/press/fill\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"snapshot_refs\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"browser_session\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"playwright_cli_session\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"interaction_result\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"script_content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nif ! command -v npx >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n  echo \\\"Error: npx is required but not found on PATH.\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nhas_session_flag=\\\"false\\\"\\nfor arg in \\\"$@\\\"; do\\n  case \\\"$arg\\\" in\\n    --session|--session=*)\\n      has_session_flag=\\\"true\\\"\\n      break\\n      ;;\\n  esac\\ndone\\n\\ncmd=(npx --yes --package @playwright/cli playwright-cli)\\nif [[ \\\"${has_session_flag}\\\" != \\\"true\\\" && -n \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION:-}\\\" ]]; then\\n  cmd+=(--session \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION}\\\")\\nfi\\ncmd+=(\\\"$@\\\")\\n\\nexec \\\"${cmd[@]}\\\"\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_interact\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"assess_resnapshot\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Determine whether another snapshot is needed\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"Snapshot again after: navigation; clicking elements that change the UI substantially; opening/closing modals or menus; tab switches.\",\n        \"Refs can go stale. When a command fails due to a missing ref, snapshot again.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"assess_need_for_resnapshot\",\n          \"opcode\": \"assess_need_for_resnapshot\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"interaction_result\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"needs_resnapshot\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_resnapshot_decision\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"needs_resnapshot\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"assess_artifact_usefulness\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Determine whether capturing artifacts is useful\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"assess_artifact_usefulness\",\n          \"opcode\": \"assess_artifact_usefulness\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"artifacts_useful\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_artifact_decision\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"artifacts_useful\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"capture_artifacts\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Capture browser artifacts when useful\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [\n        \"When capturing artifacts in this repo, use `output/playwright/` and avoid introducing new top-level artifact folders.\"\n      ],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"capture_browser_artifacts\",\n          \"opcode\": \"execute_playwright_cli_wrapper\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"pwcli_path\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"literal\",\n              \"literal_value\": \"screenshot/pdf/traces\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"output/playwright/\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"external_resource\",\n              \"identifier\": \"browser_session\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"playwright_cli_session\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"script_content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nif ! command -v npx >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n  echo \\\"Error: npx is required but not found on PATH.\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nhas_session_flag=\\\"false\\\"\\nfor arg in \\\"$@\\\"; do\\n  case \\\"$arg\\\" in\\n    --session|--session=*)\\n      has_session_flag=\\\"true\\\"\\n      break\\n      ;;\\n  esac\\ndone\\n\\ncmd=(npx --yes --package @playwright/cli playwright-cli)\\nif [[ \\\"${has_session_flag}\\\" != \\\"true\\\" && -n \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION:-}\\\" ]]; then\\n  cmd+=(--session \\\"${PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION}\\\")\\nfi\\ncmd+=(\\\"$@\\\")\\n\\nexec \\\"${cmd[@]}\\\"\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_after_capture\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"finish\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Finish the browser workflow\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": null,\n      \"constraints\": [],\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"return_done\",\n          \"opcode\": \"return\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"check_npx\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"install_nodejs\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"npx is not available\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"check_npx\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"setup_wrapper\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"npx is available\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"install_nodejs\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"check_npx\",\n      \"condition_text\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"setup_wrapper\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"read_session_env\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"read_session_env\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"choose_reference\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"choose_reference\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"read_cli_reference\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"CLI command reference needed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"choose_reference\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"read_workflows_reference\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"workflows/troubleshooting reference needed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"choose_reference\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"open_page\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"no reference guide needed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"read_cli_reference\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"open_page\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"read_workflows_reference\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"open_page\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"open_page\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"snapshot_page\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"snapshot_page\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"interact_page\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"interact_page\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"assess_resnapshot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"assess_resnapshot\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"snapshot_page\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"navigation, significant DOM change, modal/menu change, tab switch, stale refs, or missing-ref command failure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"assess_resnapshot\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"assess_artifact_usefulness\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"no re-snapshot needed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"assess_artifact_usefulness\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"capture_artifacts\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"artifacts useful\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"assess_artifact_usefulness\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"finish\",\n      \"condition_text\": \"artifacts not useful\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_block_ref\": \"capture_artifacts\",\n      \"target_block_ref\": \"finish\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"diagnostics\": [\n    \"Source conflict/ambiguity: SKILL.md says to prefer the bundled wrapper unless the repository standardizes on a global install; references/cli.md says to use the wrapper unless the CLI is already installed globally. Both conditions are preserved as constraints; the main workflow uses the bundled wrapper.\",\n    \"The reference section says 'Open only what you need' for two guides. The IR models a single-choice dispatch among CLI reference, workflows reference, or no reference; if both are needed, the source does not specify an order or merge.\",\n    \"The core workflow does not define a termination condition for the interaction/re-snapshot loop. The IR exits when no re-snapshot is needed and then assesses whether artifact capture is useful.\",\n    \"Session isolation is described in references/cli.md and references/workflows.md but not in the core SKILL.md workflow. The IR reads PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_SESSION as an optional context key and preserves session guidance as constraints rather than a mandatory branch.\",\n    \"The CLI configuration file behavior from references/workflows.md is preserved as a constraint; it is not modeled as a separate acquisition because it is internal to the CLI tool.\"\n  ]\n}"
